# Dependencies are never vendored. This package has no runtime dependencies at all
# (the DSH plugin tree has no per-plugin isolation, so every dependency is a
# liability); the two entries under `peerDependencies` are provided by the host and
# are peers for exactly that reason.
node_modules/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Output of `node tools/preview.mjs`, which renders the real panel and screenshots it in
# light and dark. Regenerable in seconds and specific to this machine's Chrome, so the
# TOOL is committed and its output is not.
#
# `.npmignore` mirrors this, AND `package.json`'s `files` lists `tools/*.mjs` instead of the
# whole `tools/` directory: npm ignores `.npmignore` for anything a `files` entry pulled in,
# so a generated `tools/preview.html` was shipping in the tarball (with the two PNGs, 500KB
# of screenshots) until both were fixed. The tarball went 908KB -> 367KB.
tools/preview.html
tools/preview-*.png

# NOTE: `lib/client.js` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is a generated artifact, but it is also the only way someone can install this
# plugin without a build step — the target machine has no toolchain, and the whole
# point of shipping `lib/` is that "copy the folder, run one script, restart" works.
# So it is committed on purpose.
#
# If you change anything under `src/client/`, run `node tools/build-client.mjs` and
# commit the rebuilt bundle in the SAME commit. `verify-install.mjs` fails when the
# bundle does not match the package, so a forgotten rebuild is caught rather than
# shipped.

dist/
